   "daf": "40b",
   "sentenceId": 17,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ זְנַב הָעֵגֶל — שֶׁאֵינָהּ מַגַּעַת לָעַרְקוֹב, אָמְרוּ חֲכָמִים: כֹּל מַרְבִּית עֲגָלִים כֵּן, כׇּל זְמַן שֶׁיְּהוּ מְגַדְּלִין — הֵן נִמְתָּחוֹת. אֵיזֶהוּ עַרְקוֹב שֶׁאָמְרוּ? רַבִּי חֲנִינָא בֶּן אַנְטִיגְנוֹס אוֹמֵר: בְּעַרְקוֹב שֶׁבְּאֶמְצַע הַיָּרֵךְ.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» In the case of «the tail of a calf that does not reach the leg joint [la’arkov], the Sages said:» It is a blemish, because «all growth of calves» is in «this» manner:«As long as they grow,» their tails «are extended» beneath the leg joint. «Which is the leg joint» about «which» the Sages «spoke? Rabbi Ḥanina ben Antigonus says:» They are referring «to» the «leg joint that is in the middle of the thigh.»"
  }
